    "terrainName": "berlin",
    "description": "What: Simulated devices SD-S5b (§5a, D-120 / D-56). The Observer carries a laser rangefinder (kit 1) with BINOCULARS STACKED on it (mounted in the rangefinder's stacking station) and linked to receive from it. A scripted trainee possesses him, aims at a marker 450 m away, ranges it through the rangefinder and SENDs, then binds his view to the STACKED binoculars. Judge: (1) the stacked binoculars are operated by the stack's operator - the Observer's station holds them; (2) the ROOT (the rangefinder) turns to the marker with the look and measures it - the laser meets THAT marker; (3) the binoculars point where the root points: the target the rangefinder sent shows on THEIR HUD dead ahead (0 degrees off the boresight). That also proves they ignore their own look while stacked (D-56): the same look applied a second time on top of the root's would put the cue tens of degrees off. Fail: the root does not follow the look, or the stacked device points elsewhere than the root. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh dv-stacked-devices"
  },
